{
  "description": "10-30 queue on bodaborg-tpu7x-nap (spot 2x2x1 single-host slices): BEFORE qwen3.5-397b-a17b scanned on 4 slices, fix validations and to_maxtext save-memory runs. See reports/tpu7x_priority1_progress.md.",
  "notes": "before_397b_scanned_s4 is the only scanned 397B configuration that loads with Lance's PRs (1,399.7 s on 4 slices), so it gives scanned 397B a BEFORE (origin/main) point, with the 1800 s watchdog of the other BEFORE re-runs. The fix_* tasks run safetensors_dynamic from /tmp/maxtext_fix (this branch's load_dynamic.py and tensor_handling.py: each leaf of a stacked composite key is stacked on its own, and reshard slices are joined two at a time) into the run ids tpu7x_200b_fix and tpu7x_16m_fix. The tmfix_* tasks run to_maxtext with this branch's utils.py, whose Orbax save honours checkpoint_storage_concurrent_gb (the harness passes 24 for unscanned) instead of buffering up to 96 GB: tmfix_llama70b_unscanned_conv measures the save-phase peak against the P2 run (403.6 GB), and tmfix_397b_unscanned_conv retries the conversion that was OOM-killed when its save started.",
